{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/85159-lfg-masquerade-a-la-strix","id":85159,"title":"LFG- Masquerade a la Strix","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-06T00:28:24-08:00","id":85159,"title":"LFG- Masquerade a la Strix","content":"So, I'm looking for players for a pulpy, Masquerade-style game using Blood and Smoke for the major Mechanics and VtM for much of the setting and antagonists. I am almost finished converting most of the CWoD material to fit within the modern system and so far I have 2 players. I'd like to have 4-6, but I'll wait and see what kind of interest this gets. I am planning on hosting this game on the Pen and Paper Games Website, as their forums support dice actions with ease.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T18:24:04-08:00","id":87124,"title":"","content":"I am a little hesitant, having never actually played in a PBP game before, and being only casually familiar with the Masquerade setting. But I am interested, as the idea of a Masquerade game with Requiem rules (and especially B&amp;S rules) has always appealed to me. I would like a bit more details before I would be willing to commit to it though. Would this be an appropriate place to discuss such details, or would PMing work better?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T23:13:24-08:00","id":87275,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/85159-lfg-masquerade-a-la-strix?p=87124#post87124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am a little hesitant, having never actually played in a PBP game before, and being only casually familiar with the Masquerade setting. But I am interested, as the idea of a Masquerade game with Requiem rules (and especially B&amp;S rules) has always appealed to me. I would like a bit more details before I would be willing to commit to it though. Would this be an appropriate place to discuss such details, or would PMing work better?</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Here would be a fine place to discuss the details.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">\u200bCurrently, I'm in the process of upgrading the material in the Conversion Guide to better fit with B&amp;S, as well as bringing most of the non-core Bloodlines and powers up to date. Most of the bloodline disciplines are ready, but more labor-intensive elements, like Thaumaturgy, are still in the works. Becoming Antitribu has some mechanical drawbacks, as they are a kind of generic bloodline, and keeping the Kindred-Specific merits in play is a challenge. Plot's a little nebulous AtM, but I'm leaning toward a Noirish detective story.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T00:37:10-08:00","id":87318,"title":"","content":"Cool, so I assume the PCs will be Camarilla, meaning Camarilla Clans are fine, maybe Independent Clans with approval, but no Sabbat Antitribu? That's fine by me, I would undoubtedly want to play either a Ventrue or maybe a Giovanni, so no issues there. Are you planning to run it as the 13 Masquerade Clans, or the 5 Requiem Clans with the Masquerade Clans as Bloodlines? I'd love to get a look at your conversion doccuments if that's ok, so I have an idea what rules I'd be playing under.<br /> <br /> If I may make a suggestion, if you are ok with more spirit-of-the-Masquerade-rules than a direct conversion, the rules for improvising rituals from the Blood Sorcery book would make a pretty good facsimile of Thaumaturgy. Just re-brand Themes as &quot;Paths&quot; and call it a day. I have also done some homebrew conversion of Masquerade to Requiem, I'd be happy to offer you what I've got if it would help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T03:16:25-07:00","id":87391,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\">The Masquerade core 13 are Clans proper, while the bloodlines are just that, with a few corner-cases, like the Gargoyles and Blood Brothers. Tremere do not automatically gain access to Thaumaturgy, nor do Cappadocians gain Necromancy, as I feel those should be a Bloodline/Status-granted power sets. Luckily, B&amp;S's rules regarding bloodlines mesh well with the fluff of certain Clans (like the Giovanni). The one rules tweak I planned on applying to Blood Sorcery was to allow fast casting, so if you did decide to use Necromancy/Thaumaturgy, you could do more when there is no time for ritual casting. Most of the Discipline adjustments are based off of the Conversion Guide, but where something had too much redundancy (clan Baali, for example) it got replaced with its best B&amp;S equivalent. Here is what I have so far:</span><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheet/ccc?key=0AgaVV2Oc5KiIdDNMSlh0T0ZTZmhQendsbmt4dU5NUHc&amp;usp=docslist_api\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/spreadsheet/...p=docslist_api</a><br /> Any input would be appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":1959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","user":"Hexmeister Vic","date":".  courtesy 03-09-2014, 06:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T06:54:45-07:00","id":87458,"title":"","content":"Sounds pretty cool. I can't open the google doc though, it says I don't have permission to view it. you must have it set to private. I sent a request for permission to access it, <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#84d4e5f6efe1f6aae5aaeeaabdb5c4e3e9e5ede8aae7ebe9\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"144475667f71663a753a7e3a2d25547379757d783a777b79\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a><br /> <br /> EDIT: It's working now, thank you! Looking at some of this I think I'm leaning more towards Giovanni, if that's acceptable. Anyway, keep me posted on developments, I'd be happy to give it a shot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-09-2014, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-10T17:49:15-07:00","id":88525,"title":"","content":"Cool. I'll get Necromancy finished ASAP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T15:59:46-07:00","id":91155,"title":"","content":"-raises hand- I'm interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"